@startuml
autonumber
title Sequence Diagram: MES Dashboard Read & Update with Cache

actor Operator
participant "MES Frontend" as FE
participant "MES API" as API
participant "Redis (Cache)" as Cache
database "MES DB" as DB

== Scenario 1: Operator Views Dashboard (Read) ==

Operator -> FE: Open Dashboard (Status=NEW)
FE -> API: GET /orders?status=NEW
activate API

API -> Cache: GET orders:status:NEW
activate Cache
Cache --> API: (Miss) null
deactivate Cache

note right of API: Cache Miss -> Read from DB

API -> DB: SELECT * FROM orders WHERE status='NEW'
activate DB
DB --> API: Returns List[Order]
deactivate DB

API -> Cache: SET orders:status:NEW, List[Order], TTL=300s
activate Cache
Cache --> API: OK
deactivate Cache

API --> FE: Returns List[Order]
deactivate API
FE --> Operator: Shows Orders List

== Scenario 2: Operator Updates Order Status (Write) ==

Operator -> FE: Click "Start Work" (Order ID=123)
FE -> API: POST /orders/123/status {status: IN_PROGRESS}
activate API

API -> DB: UPDATE orders SET status='IN_PROGRESS' WHERE id=123
activate DB
DB --> API: OK
deactivate DB

note right of API: Write-Strategy: Invalidate related keys

API -> Cache: DEL orders:status:NEW
activate Cache
Cache --> API: OK
deactivate Cache

API -> Cache: DEL orders:status:IN_PROGRESS
activate Cache
Cache --> API: OK
deactivate Cache

API --> FE: 200 OK
deactivate API

== Scenario 3: Operator Refreshes Dashboard (Read after Write) ==

FE -> API: GET /orders?status=NEW
activate API
API -> Cache: GET orders:status:NEW
activate Cache
Cache --> API: (Miss) null
deactivate Cache

API -> DB: SELECT * FROM orders WHERE status='NEW'
activate DB
DB --> API: Returns Updated List
deactivate DB

API -> Cache: SET orders:status:NEW, Updated List
activate Cache
deactivate Cache

API --> FE: Updated List
deactivate API

@enduml